E["npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Light's Hope Chapel, Lord Maxwell Tyrosus directs the Argent Dawn's defense against the Scourge. A veteran paladin of the Silver Hand, he also sends forces against blighted strongholds such as Stratholme.",h="At Light's Hope Chapel, Lord Maxwell Tyrosus directs the Argent Dawn's defense against the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Veteran of Lordaeron",b="In the Third War, Maxwell Tyrosus rode with Uther the Lightbringer. He guarded Andorhal's exits as the Scourge tore through the kingdom. After Lordaeron fell, Tyrosus joined the Argent Dawn. The order welcomes anyone willing to fight the Scourge, unlike the Scarlet Crusade and its human-only zealotry.",sp=0},{t="Commander of the Dawn",b="Tyrosus leads the Argent Dawn and directs the defenses of Light's Hope Chapel. From his command post inside the chapel, he oversees military operations across the Plaguelands. Among them are tactical assaults led by Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff against Baron Rivendare in the ruins of Stratholme.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Maxwell Tyrosus?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus is a veteran human paladin who leads the Argent Dawn. He fought under Uther the Lightbringer during the Third War. Now he commands Light's Hope Chapel's defense and the order's campaign to cleanse the Plaguelands.",al={"who is maxwell tyrosus","tyrosus lore","leader of argent dawn","argent dawn boss"}},{q="Why did Tyrosus leave the Scarlet Crusade?",a="No record places Tyrosus among the Scarlet Crusade. He leads the Argent Dawn, an order that welcomes any race willing to fight the Scourge, unlike the Crusade's human-only zealotry.",al={"why did tyrosus leave scarlet crusade","tyrosus scarlet crusade","is tyrosus scarlet crusade"}},{q="Where can Maxwell Tyrosus be found?",a="You can find Maxwell Tyrosus inside the sanctuary of Light's Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn's fortified stronghold in the far eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"tyrosus location","where is maxwell tyrosus","tyrosus map"}},{q="What is Tyrosus's role in the war against Stratholme?",a="Tyrosus coordinates military strategy with Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff. He sends proven adventurers and strike teams to breach Stratholme and eliminate Baron Rivendare, the Lich King's commander in the region.",al={"tyrosus stratholme","tyrosus rivendare"}},{q="Does Tyrosus allow anyone to meet with him?",a="Tyrosus rarely grants audiences to outsiders. He has spent years secluded in war councils, directing the frontline effort. Adventurers usually need to earn the Argent Dawn's deep respect or bring critical intelligence to gain his attention.",al={"can i talk to tyrosus","tyrosus audience"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see Tyrosus uphold the Silver Hand's spirit through compassion, unity, and discipline after Uther's death and the tragic corruption of the order's splinter factions.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though born a nobleman of Lordaeron and a hero of the Alliance, Tyrosus now commits his forces to an independent order that welcomes anyone willing to fight the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="Unlike the zealots in Hearthglen and the Scarlet Monastery, Tyrosus champions cooperation with non-humans. Horde warriors and shamans are accepted as equals within Light's Hope Chapel."},kw={"argent dawn","light's hope chapel","paladin","scourge","silver hand","stratholme","tyrosus"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","npc:tirion-fordring"},src={"Lord Maxwell Tyrosus"}}
E["npc:nathanos-blightcaller"] = {t="npc",n="Nathanos Blightcaller",z="easternplaguelands",s="At the ruined Marris Stead in the Eastern Plaguelands, Nathanos Blightcaller guards the frontier for Queen Sylvanas Windrunner. Once the only human Ranger Lord of Quel'Thalas, he now trains Forsaken hunters and greets those who approach with biting contempt.",h="At the ruined Marris Stead in the Eastern Plaguelands, Nathanos Blightcaller guards the frontier for Queen...",sec={{t="The Only Human Farstrider",b="Nathanos Marris was raised on Lordaeron's rural outskirts and became a master marksman and a gifted tactician. The high elves of Quel'Thalas trained him, and he grew close to Sylvanas Windrunner. He alone among humans earned the rank of Ranger Lord. The Marris Stead remained his family home.",sp=0},{t="The Fall and Rebirth",b="After Prince Arthas and the Scourge swept through Lordaeron following the purge of Stratholme, plague consumed the kingdom. Nathanos made a desperate stand at the Marris Stead, where Ramstein the Gorger, a monstrous abomination, killed him. Raised as a mindless undead thrall, he roamed the blighted fields and slew in the Lich King's name.\n\nSylvanas broke the Scourge's hold and established the Forsaken in the Undercity. She came for Nathanos, just as he had somehow known she would, and freed his mind from the Lich King's will. His tactical brilliance and fiery loyalty returned, and he joined her side.",sp=0},{t="Champion of the Banshee Queen",b="Nathanos Blightcaller lives at the ruined Marris Stead in the contested Eastern Plaguelands, guarded by foul plaguehounds. As Sylvanas's champion, he trains hunters and gathers intelligence in the region. Alliance leaders know he survived and fear his command of undead forces threatens human survival. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon sends strike forces to kill the fallen Ranger Lord.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nathanos Blightcaller?",a="Nathanos Blightcaller was Nathanos Marris, a renowned human marksman and the only human ever to become a Ranger Lord of Quel'Thalas. After he died and rose during the Third War, Sylvanas freed his mind from the Scourge. He now fights as her champion and trains hunters at his ancestral home in the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"who is nathanos","nathanos lore","who is the guy at marris stead"}},{q="Why is Nathanos at the Marris Stead?",a="The Marris Stead was Nathanos's home in life, and he fell there defending Lordaeron. In undeath, he returned to the ruined estate to train Forsaken hunters and watch Alliance and Scourge movements.",al={"where is nathanos","why is nathanos in plaguelands","marris stead nathanos"}},{q="How did Nathanos become an undead?",a="The Scourge abomination Ramstein the Gorger killed Nathanos at his homestead during the Third War. He rose as a mindless thrall to the Lich King until Sylvanas came for him and freed his mind. Then he joined the Forsaken.",al={"how did nathanos die","who killed nathanos","nathanos death"}},{q="Why does the Alliance want to kill him?",a="Stormwind's leaders learned that Nathanos Marris, one of the Alliance's greatest military minds and tactical geniuses, had survived death and joined the Forsaken. Highlord Bolvar Fordragon sees his tactical brilliance as a grave danger and orders his death.",al={"why kill nathanos","alliance quest nathanos","order must be restored"}},{q="What is his relationship with Sylvanas?",a="Nathanos was close to Sylvanas in life, when the elves of Quel'Thalas made him their only human Ranger Lord. Now he fights as her champion, with absolute and unwavering loyalty to the Banshee Queen.",al={"sylvanas and nathanos","did sylvanas love nathanos","nathanos sylvanas romance"}},{q="Who are the hounds standing near him?",a="The hounds are vicious plaguehounds Nathanos trained himself. They guard the Marris Stead ruins at his side and attack intruders who trespass on his territory.",al={"nathanos dogs","marris stead hounds","blightcaller pets"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can learn from the Forsaken's highest-ranking trainer. Nathanos brings Quel'Thalas's rigorous Farstrider marksmanship to Lordaeron's undead.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you share the Forsaken's bitter resilience, embodied by their champion Nathanos. He has little patience for incompetence among his peers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you face a decorated Lordaeron hero and celebrated Farstrider who now fights for the Forsaken. His presence insults Stormwind and poses a lethal tactical threat.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde member, you can seek Nathanos's tactical guidance and hunter training in the Plaguelands. He greets visitors with caustic disdain."},kw={"blightcaller","farstrider","hunter trainer","marris","marris stead","nathanos","plaguelands","sylvanas"},rel={"subzone:marris-stead","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","subzone:stratholme","zone:undercity"},src={"Nathanos Blightcaller"}}
E["npc:tirion-fordring"] = {t="npc",n="Tirion Fordring",z="easternplaguelands",s="Beside the Thondroril River, Tirion Fordring watches Lordaeron's tragedy unfold from exile. Once a paladin and lord of Mardenholde Keep, he lost his title and lands for honoring an oath to an enemy orc. Now he worries for his son.",h="Beside the Thondroril River, Tirion Fordring watches Lordaeron's tragedy unfold from exile.",sec={{t="A Knight of the Silver Hand",b="Before Lordaeron fell, Tirion Fordring was among its finest knights. He served as a paladin of the Knights of the Silver Hand, founded by Archbishop Alonsus Faol during the Second War. With plate, hammer, and faith in the Holy Light, he fought the Old Horde. His fellow knights revered him as a steadfast example of the Light's power.",sp=0},{t="A Matter of Honor and Exile",b="After the Second War, Tirion governed Hearthglen from Mardenholde Keep with his wife Karandra and their young son Taelan. Then he met Eitrigg, an aged orc warrior living as a hermit, and saw honor in him. Tirion promised to protect Eitrigg.\n\nWhen Alliance authorities found the orc, Tirion fought his own countrymen to keep that oath. The Alliance of Lordaeron stripped Tirion of his nobility, and the Silver Hand cast him out. He was banished, while Uther spared Karandra and Taelan from the sentence.",sp=0},{t="A Father's Torment",b="After Tirion's exile, Taelan remained in Hearthglen with his mother. Lordaeron fell to the Scourge during the Third War, and Taelan grew to manhood and joined the Scarlet Crusade. In time, he became Hearthglen's Highlord. From afar, Tirion watches the Crusade descend into madness. He grieves that fanaticism has made his son its puppet. Memories of happier days, including family visits to Caer Darrow, keep Tirion searching for a way to remind Taelan of true honor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Tirion Fordring?",a="Tirion Fordring once governed Hearthglen and served as a paladin of the Knights of the Silver Hand. His peers exiled him for defending an orc out of honor. He now lives in a cabin on the western edge of the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"tirion lore","who is the old paladin","who is tirion","hermit paladin"}},{q="Why was Tirion exiled from Lordaeron?",a="Tirion met Eitrigg, an aged orc veteran, and recognized his sense of honor. When Alliance forces found Eitrigg, Tirion fought his own comrades to keep his promise to protect him. The Alliance stripped Tirion of his titles and banished him from the kingdom.",al={"why was tirion banished","tirion treason","why is tirion an exile"}},{q="What is Tirion's connection to Hearthglen?",a="Hearthglen was Tirion's seat, and he governed it from Mardenholde Keep until his exile. His son, Highlord Taelan Fordring, commands the Scarlet Crusade there.",al={"tirion hearthglen","mardenholde keep tirion","hearthglen lord"}},{q="Does Tirion still have his paladin powers?",a="The Church and the Silver Hand stripped Tirion of his rank and claimed to revoke his holy powers. Yet his conviction kept his bond with the Holy Light unbroken. The Light still answers his will as strongly as ever.",al={"did tirion lose the light","is tirion still a paladin","does tirion use the light"}},{q="What does Tirion want with the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Tirion wants to reach his son Taelan, a high commander of the Scarlet Crusade in Hearthglen. He hopes to awaken Taelan's conscience and free him from the Crusade's corruption before his soul is lost.",al={"tirion scarlet crusade","tirion and taelan","why does tirion care about the crusade"}},{q="Who are the other original paladins?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the Knights of the Silver Hand during the Second War, with Uther the Lightbringer as its first paladin. Tirion's fellow knights included Turalyon and his close friend Saidan Dathrohan.",al={"first paladins","original silver hand paladins","alonsus faol paladins"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you stand before a knight of the Silver Hand from the Second War. He mastered the Holy Light and honored an oath above mortal law.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you meet a hero of the Alliance of Lordaeron who ruled Hearthglen justly. He recalls the noble kingdom that fell into rot and madness.",["race:Orc"]="As an orc, you meet a former enemy who slew many in the Second War. He surrendered his land, family, and name rather than break an oath of honor to Eitrigg.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you meet a man who held to the Alliance's ideals. Its kingdoms branded him a traitor for placing personal honor above racial hatred."},kw={"alonsus faol","eitrigg","exile","fordring","hearthglen","mardenholde","silver hand","taelan","thondroril","tirion"},rel={"topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","subzone:hearthglen","subzone:mardenholde-keep","npc:eitrigg","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:second-war","subzone:caer-darrow","zone:westernplaguelands"},src={"Tirion Fordring"}}
E["subzone:blackwood-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Blackwood Lake",z="easternplaguelands",s="In southern Eastern Plaguelands, a small Argent Dawn camp watches Blackwood Lake. Its waters teem with hostile, corrupted elementals and hold memories of tragedy and war.",h="In southern Eastern Plaguelands, a small Argent Dawn camp watches Blackwood Lake.",sec={{t="A Polluted Memory",b="The plague that poisons much of the Eastweald has reached Blackwood Lake. Diseased water elementals churn beneath its murky surface and attack anyone who comes near the shore.",sp=0},{t="Relics of the Fallen",b="Blackwood Lake holds grim relics from the Battle of Darrowshire. The Extended Annals of Darrowshire record that the severed skull of Horgus the Ravager was cast into its rancid depths.\n\nNearby, an Argent Dawn medic tends battered infantry at a small forward outpost. The medic struggles to keep soldiers alive amid the Scourge's devastation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What creatures lurk in Blackwood Lake?",a="Corrupted water elementals infest Blackwood Lake. Necromantic runoff and filth have twisted the Plaguelands' freshwater spirits into violent, toxic beings.",al={"what is in the water","lake monsters","elementals in blackwood lake"}},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn stationed at the lake?",a="The Argent Dawn keeps a small field camp near Blackwood Lake. There, an Argent Medic cares for wounded infantry and supports patrols fighting along the roads between Darrowshire and nearby Scourge strongholds.",al={"argent camp","argent medic","why are there soldiers here"}},{q="What Darrowshire relic is buried in Blackwood Lake?",a="The skull of Horgus the Ravager lies in Blackwood Lake, according to the Annals of Darrowshire. Horgus was one of the primary Scourge leaders in the assault on Darrowshire. He was brought down, and his skull was hurled into the lake's depths.",al={"horgus the ravager head","quest item in lake","annals of darrowshire lake"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of Lordaeron, Blackwood Lake recalls how thoroughly the Scourge poisoned the kingdom's rural heartland.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see how the blight corrupts Lordaeron's natural elementals in Blackwood Lake's polluted waters and decaying surroundings. They need the purifying touch of the Light."},kw={"blackwood","darrowshire","elementals","horgus","lake","plaguelands"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:darrowshire","topic:argent-dawn"},src={"Blackwood Lake"}}
E["subzone:browman-mill"] = {t="subzone",n="Browman Mill",z="easternplaguelands",s="Undead now crowd Browman Mill, north of Light's Hope Chapel. Once it served Lordaeron's timber trade; now Stephen Browman remains trapped in death within his ruined workshop.",h="Undead now crowd Browman Mill, north of Light's Hope Chapel.",sec={{t="A Ruined Industry",b="Before the Third War, Browman Mill worked timber from the Eastweald for nearby towns and homesteads. Then the Scourge plague swept across Lordaeron, and the mill fell with the province. Now rotting timbers and shattered wheels lie idle while abominations, banshees, and skeletal warriors patrol the grounds. So close to Light's Hope Chapel, the ruins show how near the undead horde has come to the Argent Dawn.",sp=0},{t="The Overseer's Fate",b="Stephen Browman owned Browman Mill before the Scourge overran his estate. The Scourge killed him and raised him as a ghoul, bound to the Lich King's will. He remains in the dark mill, guarding the broken remains of his life's work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Browman Mill located?",a="Browman Mill lies in the far eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, directly north of Light's Hope Chapel.",al={"browman mill location","where is browman mill","how to find browman mill"}},{q="What kind of enemies inhabit the mill?",a="Abominations, banshees, skeletal warriors, and ghouls fill Browman Mill's grounds.",al={"browman mill mobs","who is at browman mill","what lives at browman mill"}},{q="Who was Stephen Browman?",a="Stephen Browman owned and operated the lumber mill. The Scourge killed him during Lordaeron's fall and raised him as a ghoul, bound to guard the ruined mill.",al={"who is stephen browman","stephen browman lore","browman ghoul"}},{q="Why is Browman Mill dangerous to travelers?",a="Powerful undead infest Browman Mill, making it dangerous to travelers. The mill lies a short ride north of the Argent Dawn stronghold at Light's Hope Chapel.",al={"why is browman mill dangerous","threat of browman mill"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see the desecrated mill and its tormented spirits as the evils the holy orders fight to cleanse from Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know Stephen Browman's enslavement recalls those claimed by the Lich King and denied the free will the Forsaken won."},kw={"abominations","banshees","browman mill","eastern plaguelands","light's hope chapel","lumber mill","scourge","stephen browman"},rel={"subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Browman Mill"}}
E["subzone:corin-s-crossing"] = {t="subzone",n="Corin's Crossing",z="easternplaguelands",s="The Scourge has overrun Corin's Crossing, where ruined streets mark an old meeting place in south-central Eastern Plaguelands. Once travelers passed through on their way between Stratholme, Tyr's Hand, Darrowshire, and Andorhal. Now horrors haunt the town hall and forge, and unseen watchers drift among the ruins.",h="The Scourge has overrun Corin's Crossing, where ruined streets mark an old meeting place in south-central...",sec={{t="A Shattered Crossroads",b="Before the Third War, Corin's Crossing joined the roads of eastern Lordaeron. Merchants, couriers, and pilgrims stopped at this waystation between Stratholme and the southern strongholds. The settlement stood between Lake Mereldar and the place now blighted as the Infectis Scar. When the plague swept through the province, the undead vanguard reached the town. Corin's Crossing soon fell beneath its assault.",sp=0},{t="A Haven of the Damned",b="The Scourge holds Corin's Crossing now, and wandering undead crowd its muddy streets. Rotting hulks and ghouls linger in the hollowed blacksmith shop and town hall. Scouts face another danger among the ruins. Unseen Servants drift beyond ordinary sight, pierce mundane stealth, and ambush anyone trying to slip past the main horde undetected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Corin's Crossing before the plague?",a="Before the plague, Corin's Crossing was a prosperous hub in eastern Lordaeron. Its town hall and blacksmith forge stood at the heart of a waystation between Stratholme, Tyr's Hand, Darrowshire, and Andorhal. The Scourge wiped out its people.",al={"corins crossing history","corins crossing lore","what was corins crossing"}},{q="Why is Corin's Crossing so hazardous for stealthy travelers?",a="Unseen Servants haunt Corin's Crossing as invisible phantoms bound to the Scourge. They pierce magical and mundane stealth, then surprise unwary rogues or scouts and alert nearby undead.",al={"stealth in corins crossing","unseen servants","rogue corins crossing"}},{q="What major landmarks surround the town?",a="Corin's Crossing stands in south-central Eastern Plaguelands. The blighted trench of the Infectis Scar lies nearby, and Lake Mereldar runs along the town's border.",al={"corins crossing location","where is corins crossing"}},{q="Who controls Corin's Crossing today?",a="The Scourge holds Corin's Crossing. No living defenders remain, and wandering undead soldiers and spirits swarm the settlement.",al={"who owns corins crossing","corins crossing faction"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Do not trust your shadows here. Unseen Servants roam the alleys, unseen by mortal eyes, and see through your stealth. A walk through the town square can be fatal.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see Lordaeron's heartland desecrated at Corin's Crossing. The ruins remain a wretched Scourge stronghold, mocking Stratholme's holy bastion further up the road."},kw={"corin's crossing","corins crossing","eastern plaguelands","infectis scar","lake mereldar","unseen servants"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:infectis-scar","subzone:lake-mereldar","subzone:stratholme","subzone:tyr-s-hand","subzone:darrowshire","topic:scourge"},src={"Corin's Crossing"}}
E["subzone:crown-guard-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Crown Guard Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the southern Eastern Plaguelands, blight surrounds Crown Guard Tower's ruins. The Scourge destroyed it during the invasion of Lordaeron in the Third War.",h="In the southern Eastern Plaguelands, blight surrounds Crown Guard Tower's ruins.",sec={{t="A Fallen Bulwark",b="Crown Guard Tower once watched over eastern Lordaeron as part of the Kingdom's defenses. When the Scourge overran the kingdom, they destroyed the tower and left it in ruins. Several fallen towers lie scattered across what are now the Eastern Plaguelands. Charred stones remain here in a land still held by the undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Crown Guard Tower originally built for?",a="Crown Guard Tower was built as a regional military watchtower and scout outpost for the human Kingdom of Lordaeron before the Third War. It guarded the roads against incursions.",al={"crown guard tower history","why was it built","lordaeron tower"}},{q="Why is the tower ruined?",a="The Scourge destroyed Crown Guard Tower during their invasion of Lordaeron. Waves of undead overran the kingdom's defenses and left the structure in rubble.",al={"who destroyed crown guard tower","what happened here"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Crown Guard Tower's ruins recall how completely the Scourge broke the Kingdom of Lordaeron's defenses."},kw={"crown guard tower","eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","scourge","scout tower","watchtower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Crown Guard Tower"}}
E["subzone:darrowshire"] = {t="subzone",n="Darrowshire",z="easternplaguelands",s="Darrowshire lies in ruins in the southern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands. Once a peaceful hamlet of Lordaeron, it made a desperate stand against the Scourge during the Third War. Shattered timbers, restless spirits, and bitter memories remain.",h="Darrowshire lies in ruins in the southern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Tragic Stand",b="Darrowshire's villagers fought the Scourge during the Third War. Before plague consumed northern Lordaeron, the humble settlement stood beneath the southern cliffs. Marduk Blackpool, a death knight, and Horgus the Ravager, a ghoul lord, led the besieging force.\n\nThe villagers and local defenders held the line for a time, though the odds were impossible. Then their defense broke, and the Scourge slaughtered the town down to the last soul. Many fallen defenders were raised as ghouls to swell the Scourge's ranks. Darrowshire remains an empty memorial to those who died there.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Battle",b="Darrowshire's ruins still bear the weight of the slaughter. The living abandoned the village long ago, but spectral remnants of its townspeople remain trapped there. Travelers report strange sights, including ghostly reenactments of the battle unfolding in silence. Sorrow still clings to the ground, a reminder of what the Scourge took from the kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Darrowshire?",a="The Scourge destroyed Darrowshire during the Third War. Marduk Blackpool, a death knight, and Horgus the Ravager, a ghoul lord, led the assault. Their forces overwhelmed the defenders and slaughtered the inhabitants, leaving the village in ruins.",al={"darrowshire history","why is darrowshire destroyed","what happened here"}},{q="Who were the leaders of the Scourge attack on Darrowshire?",a="Marduk Blackpool, a death knight, and Horgus the Ravager, a ghoul lord, led the Scourge assault on Darrowshire. Their forces broke the village's defenders and destroyed the settlement.",al={"who attacked darrowshire","darrowshire villains","horgus and marduk"}},{q="Why is Darrowshire haunted?",a="The slaughter bound the spirits of Darrowshire's fallen to the earth. Ghostly figures linger among the ruins, and the battle itself sometimes plays out again in spectral form, leaving the dead trapped in their final moments.",al={"darrowshire ghosts","why are there spirits in darrowshire"}},{q="What became of the villagers who died defending the town?",a="The Scourge slaughtered Darrowshire's defenders, and many were reanimated as ghouls. They were forced to serve the army that destroyed their homes.",al={"darrowshire villagers","defenders of darrowshire"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="As a human of the Alliance, Darrowshire recalls the devastation inflicted on Lordaeron and the ordinary folk who made a hopeless stand to defend their families.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can bring the purifying Light to the Plaguelands, strike down the undead, and lay tortured spirits to rest."},kw={"battle of darrowshire","darrowshire","eastern plaguelands","ghouls","horgus the ravager","lordaeron","marduk blackpool"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:third-war","npc:nathanos-blightcaller"},src={"Darrowshire"}}
E["subzone:eastwall-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastwall Gate",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Stratholme’s eastern wall, Eastwall Gate offers a way into the ruined city. It lies in northern Eastern Plaguelands, apart from the chaos at the main gates.",h="At Stratholme’s eastern wall, Eastwall Gate offers a way into the ruined city.",sec={{t="The Back Door to Ruin",b="Eastwall Gate cuts through Stratholme’s eastern fortifications. The main entrance opens onto King’s Square, but this barred passage leads to Elders’ Square near the steps of Alonsus Chapel. From there, you can enter the city’s depths without passing the front barricades or the undead lines.",sp=0},{t="Through the Iron Lattice",b="Heavy ironwork seals Eastwall Gate. The Key to the City, found inside Stratholme, opens it, and an infiltrator skilled enough can pick its masterwork locks. A mechanical lever on the inner wall raises the portcullis so allies can follow.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Eastwall Gate lead?",a="Eastwall Gate opens into Elders’ Square in ruined Stratholme, near Alonsus Chapel.",al={"where does eastwall gate go","eastwall gate destination","what is behind eastwall gate"}},{q="How can the gate be opened?",a="Eastwall Gate is locked. The Key to the City, found inside Stratholme, opens it, or an expert rogue can pick the lock. A lever inside raises the portcullis.",al={"how to open eastwall gate","unlock eastwall gate","eastwall gate key"}},{q="Why would adventurers use this entrance over the main gate?",a="Eastwall Gate lets strike teams bypass the infested front streets and enter near Elders’ Square. From there, they can reach particular quarters of the city more quickly.",al={"why use eastwall gate","side entrance benefits","why side gate stratholme"}},{q="Can you open the gate from the inside?",a="Yes. A lever on Stratholme’s side raises Eastwall Gate and lets others through without a key.",al={"lever inside eastwall gate","open eastwall gate from inside"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you need masterful lockpicking to open Eastwall Gate without the Key to the City.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you emerge near Alonsus Chapel, a holy sanctuary amid the Scourge’s ashes and horrors."},kw={"alonsus chapel","eastern plaguelands","eastwall gate","elders' square","key to the city","portcullis","side entrance","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Eastwall Gate"}}
E["subzone:eastwall-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Eastwall Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="On the eastern road, Eastwall Tower watches over a wilderness still infested with Scourge. Built as a scout tower for Lordaeron, it fell when the Scourge swept across the kingdom during the Third War.",h="On the eastern road, Eastwall Tower watches over a wilderness still infested with Scourge.",sec={{t="A Ruined Watch on the Border",b="Eastwall Tower's broken ramparts look down on roads through Scourge-infested countryside. Built to guard Lordaeron's border, it watched travelers bound for the far reaches of the realm. When the Scourge invaded during the Third War, the outpost fell with the settlements around it. Shattered stone arches and burnt timber remain.\n\nThe Lich King's armies still infest the region. From its high ground, the ruined tower overlooks the eastern roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Eastwall Tower before it fell?",a="Before it fell, Eastwall Tower was a defensive scout tower built by the Kingdom of Lordaeron. It formed part of the border watch, guarding trade routes and outlying farms before the Third War brought Lordaeron's fall.",al={"eastwall tower history","who built eastwall tower","what was this place"}},{q="Who destroyed the tower?",a="The Scourge destroyed Eastwall Tower during Prince Arthas Menethil's conquest and the undead ravaging of Lordaeron that followed. Undead monstrosities smashed its defenses, killed the defenders and left the tower in ruins.",al={"how was eastwall tower ruined","what happened to eastwall tower"}},{q="Why is the tower strategically important?",a="Even in ruins, Eastwall Tower commands high ground along the eastern roads of the Plaguelands. From there, it overlooks Scourge-infested countryside.",al={"eastwall tower importance","eastwall tower position"}},{q="Is the tower safe to rest at?",a="Eastwall Tower stands in Scourge-infested countryside and offers no secure refuge.",al={"can i rest here","friendly guards"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, retaking Eastwall Tower honors Lordaeron's fallen soldiers and secures the approach to Light's Hope Chapel against Scourge incursions.",["faction:Horde"]="The ruined scout tower overlooks roads through the hostile northern lands."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","eastwall tower","lordaeron","plaguelands tower","scout tower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Eastwall Tower"}}
E["subzone:fungal-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Fungal Vale",z="easternplaguelands",s="In Fungal Vale, Scourge horrors roam beneath a murky haze, and Cult of the Damned acolytes serve among the fungi. The vale lies in south-central Eastern Plaguelands, north of Crown Guard Tower and Marris Stead.",h="In Fungal Vale, Scourge horrors roam beneath a murky haze, and Cult of the Damned acolytes serve among the...",sec={{t="A Garden of Rot",b="North of Marris Stead, Fungal Vale lies among Lordaeron’s most corrupted places. Sickly purple earth swells with alien fungi beneath a haze of necrotic spores. The Plague of Undeath has warped the soil, raising unholy growths that feed carrion beasts and shambling undead. Members of the Cult of the Damned tend the blighted blooms and perform foul rites amid the decay.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fungal Vale?",a="Fungal Vale is a corrupted valley in the southern Eastern Plaguelands, north of Crown Guard Tower and Marris Stead. The Plague of Undeath has blighted the land and turned ordinary vegetation into sprawling fungal growths.",al={"where is fungal vale","fungal vale lore","fungal vale overview"}},{q="Why is the ground purple here?",a="The Plague of Undeath has saturated the soil with necrotic power. It twists the land into ground fertile with virulent spores and stains the earth a bruised purple.",al={"why is the ground purple","purple dirt plaguelands","fungal vale ground"}},{q="Who controls this area?",a="Scourge horrors and mortal cultists of the Cult of the Damned hold Fungal Vale. Undead wander through the haze while acolytes tend its corrupted fungi.",al={"who is in fungal vale","fungal vale enemies","cultists fungal vale"}},{q="Where is it located relative to local landmarks?",a="Fungal Vale lies in south-central Eastern Plaguelands, north of the road between Marris Stead and Crown Guard Tower.",al={"how to get to fungal vale","fungal vale location","near crown guard tower"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see nature’s cycle mocked in Fungal Vale, where the Scourge have replaced life with unending, unholy rot.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you see necromancy blighting Lordaeron’s native plants and choking the ground with fungi."},kw={"blight","crown guard tower","cult of the damned","eastern plaguelands","fungal vale","fungus","marris stead","plague of undeath","scourge"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:marris-stead","topic:cult-of-the-damned","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge"},src={"Fungal Vale"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-arms-tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Arms (Tyr's Hand)",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scarlet fighters hold the Hall of Arms in Tyr's Hand, deep in the southeastern Plaguelands. This wing of Tyr's Hand Abbey houses the crusade's martial vanguard, across the abbey from its library.",h="Scarlet fighters hold the Hall of Arms in Tyr's Hand, deep in the southeastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Steel",b="Scarlet fighters keep watch in the Hall of Arms, south of Tyr's Hand Abbey's main hall. Their armory and quarters fill this wing, while archives and holy texts are kept opposite. The defenders wear heavy armor and swear to destroy the undead and anyone they judge impure. As horrors surround them in the Plaguelands, they guard the abbey and keep their weapons and shields ready.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Arms located?",a="The Hall of Arms lies within Tyr's Hand Abbey, in Tyr's Hand in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. It forms the abbey's southern wing, opposite the Library Wing.",al={"hall of arms location","where is hall of arms","tyrs hand abbey hall of arms"}},{q="Who occupies the Hall of Arms?",a="Elite Scarlet Crusade fighters hold the Hall of Arms. Warriors, paladins, and guards tend their weapons there and prepare to fight the Scourge and outsiders who enter their sanctuary.",al={"who lives in hall of arms","hall of arms enemies","scarlet crusade hall of arms"}},{q="What is the purpose of this wing compared to the rest of the abbey?",a="The Hall of Arms houses troops, weapons, and the work of keeping both ready for battle. Across the abbey, the opposite wing is devoted to study, contemplation, and scripture. Here, the defenders prepare against Scourge attacks.",al={"purpose of hall of arms","what is hall of arms for"}},{q="Can members of the Alliance enter peacefully?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade in Tyr's Hand attacks Alliance and Horde travelers on sight. Though they share human roots and venerate the Holy Light, they see outsiders as possible plague carriers or allies of evil.",al={"is scarlet crusade friendly to alliance","can alliance visit hall of arms","will tyrs hand attack me"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For a knight of the Silver Hand, the Hall of Arms is a bitter sight: sacred traditions of holy combat turned toward zealous isolation.",["class:Warrior"]="The Hall of Arms shows human arms and disciplined preparation for battle at their peak. Yet fanaticism directs their use."},kw={"abbey","armory","eastern plaguelands","hall of arms","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand","tyrs hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Hall of Arms (Tyr's Hand)"}}
E["subzone:infectis-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Infectis Scar",z="easternplaguelands",s="Near Corin's Crossing, the Infectis Scar remains open in the blighted earth of the Eastern Plaguelands. Necromantic power split the ground when a cursed runeblade broke against a dwarven shield, and blight still festers below.",h="Near Corin's Crossing, the Infectis Scar remains open in the blighted earth of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Wound of Dark Magic",b="Near Corin's Crossing, a jagged chasm cuts through the Plaguelands. The Pestilent Scar began as natural terrain and was poisoned by plague, but this wound opened during the Third War. Death knight Marduk Blackpool clashed with a dwarf captain, and his cursed runesword shattered against the captain's shield.\n\nMarduk discarded the broken weapon but kept its hilt. The severed blade sank into the soil, and its foul enchantment tore open the earth. Blight still festers at the bottom of the scar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How was the Infectis Scar formed?",a="The Infectis Scar opened in a battle near Corin's Crossing. Death knight Marduk Blackpool's runesword broke against a dwarven captain's shield, and the shattered blade sank into the earth. Its dark magic tore open a rift.",al={"infectis scar origin","how did infectis scar happen","who made the infectis scar"}},{q="How is it different from the Pestilent Scar?",a="The Pestilent Scar began as a natural gorge, then the Scourge's plague corrupted it. Marduk Blackpool's broken runeblade blasted open the Infectis Scar with its malevolent sorcery.",al={"difference between infectis and pestilent scar","pestilent scar comparison"}},{q="Who was Marduk Blackpool?",a="Marduk Blackpool, known as the Black, served the Scourge as a death knight. He took part in the slaughter across Lordaeron, including the assault on Darrowshire and skirmishes around Corin's Crossing.",al={"marduk blackpool","who is marduk"}},{q="Where is the sword now?",a="The shattered runeblade sank deep into the chasm it created. Marduk Blackpool kept the hilt after the clash.",al={"runeblade location","where is the blade"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see how an unnamed dwarf captain's shield held firm against a death knight's dark runeblade. The cursed steel shattered, and its fall carved the scar.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can sense corrupting necromantic sorcery in the chasm. Cursed runes can desecrate the earth when severed from their wielder."},kw={"chasm","corin's crossing","darrowshire","infectis scar","marduk blackpool","pestilent scar","runesword"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:corin-s-crossing","subzone:pestilent-scar","subzone:darrowshire","topic:dwarf"},src={"Infectis Scar"}}
E["subzone:lake-mereldar"] = {t="subzone",n="Lake Mereldar",z="easternplaguelands",s="Lake Mereldar's waters south of Corin's Crossing have turned foul and corrupted. Once part of Lordaeron's rural heartland, the lake now breeds twisted elementals beneath the Scourge's lingering taint.",h="Lake Mereldar's waters south of Corin's Crossing have turned foul and corrupted.",sec={{t="A Polluted Haven",b="South of Corin's Crossing, Lake Mereldar rests among the old farms of northern Lordaeron. Ruins of a homestead, an abandoned shack, and a worn ferry mark its shores. Farmers and travelers once crossed its gentle waters by ferry.\n\nThen the Scourge brought its plague of undeath, and the lake and its surroundings fell into ruin. The soil withered, and the water turned foul and poisonous.",sp=0},{t="Twisted Inhabitants",b="The blight in Lake Mereldar has tainted the water and the spirits bound to it. Blighted Surges are corrupted water elementals, driven mad by necromantic residue. They lurk in the shallows and surface without warning.\n\nPlague Ravagers prowl the muddy, weed-choked banks. They hunt living creatures that stray near the dead shoreline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Lake Mereldar located?",a="Lake Mereldar lies in the central-southern Eastern Plaguelands, directly south of Corin's Crossing.",al={"mereldar location","where is lake mereldar","find lake mereldar"}},{q="Why are there water elementals in the lake?",a="Blighted Surges are water elementals twisted into hostile creatures by necromantic blight that seeped into the lake during Lordaeron's fall.",al={"blighted surge","water elementals mereldar","corrupted elementals"}},{q="Who owned the shack and ferry on the shore?",a="The shack and ferry belonged to a local farming homestead established before the Third War. When the plague ravaged the Eastweald, the homesteaders perished or fled, leaving them to rot.",al={"ferry ruins","mereldar house","abandoned dock"}},{q="Is the water safe to drink or swim in?",a="No. The plague of undeath fouls the lake, making its water dangerous to drink, swim in, or harvest from. Blighted creatures dwell there too.",al={"can you drink the water","is lake mereldar poisoned"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how the Scourge's foul magic twists natural elemental spirits into mindless, violent horrors like the Blighted Surges of Lake Mereldar."},kw={"blighted surge","corin's crossing","eastern plaguelands","elementals","ferry","lake mereldar","plague ravager"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:corin-s-crossing"},src={"Lake Mereldar"}}
E["subzone:library-wing-tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Library Wing (Tyr's Hand)",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the Library Wing of Tyr's Hand, Scarlet Crusaders guard their books and relics. The secluded hall lies within the order's fortified redoubt in the Eastern Plaguelands. Crusaders gather there to study scripture and keep watch over the sanctum.",h="In the Library Wing of Tyr's Hand, Scarlet Crusaders guard their books and relics.",sec={{t="Sanctum of Zealous Lore",b="Off the abbey's central nave and opposite the martial quarters, the Library Wing holds the Scarlet Crusade's religious writings. Priests and crusaders study theology, militant doctrine, and works shaped by years of war against the Scourge.\n\nThese books do not preserve open scholarship. They feed the Crusade's suspicion and its belief that every outsider bears corruption.",sp=0},{t="Vessels of the Light",b="The Scarlet priesthood guards the library's scrolls and scriptures. To reach its back rooms, you must fight through elite Scarlet defenders. They protect the library as both a bastion of faith and a fortress.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library Wing located?",a="The Library Wing lies inside Tyr's Hand Abbey, in the Scarlet Crusade enclave of Tyr's Hand in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands. Within the abbey, it is south of the main entrance hall and opposite the Hall of Arms.",al={"library wing location","where is the library wing","how to find library wing tyr's hand"}},{q="What kinds of books are kept here?",a="The shelves hold theology devoted to the Holy Light, militant doctrines, and Scarlet Crusade writings meant to justify its endless crusade against the undead and outsiders.",al={"what books are in the library","tyr's hand library tomes","what is stored in the library wing"}},{q="Who controls this part of the abbey?",a="Elite Scarlet Crusade forces control the Library Wing. Clerics, scholars, and heavily armed defenders guard its doctrinal texts and sanctified supplies.",al={"who is in the library wing","who controls the library wing"}},{q="Is the Library Wing dangerous to visit?",a="Yes. The Library Wing lies deep within Tyr's Hand, a Scarlet Crusade stronghold where its zealous defenders attack trespassers on sight.",al={"is the library wing safe","tyr's hand library difficulty"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can see how the Library Wing turns divine contemplation toward narrow-minded extremism and paranoia.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may see the Library Wing as a perversion of the Silver Hand's scholarly traditions, where devotion to the Light has given way to militant zealotry."},kw={"abbey","eastern plaguelands","library wing","propaganda","scarlet crusade","tomes","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Library Wing (Tyr's Hand)"}}
E["subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"] = {t="subzone",n="Light's Hope Chapel",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Light's Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn holds its chief redoubt against the Scourge. In the eastern Plaguelands, the Church of the Holy Light's secluded Eastweald chapel has become the order's headquarters.",h="At Light's Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn holds its chief redoubt against the Scourge.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Plaguelands",b="Light's Hope Chapel began as a secluded chapel of the Church of the Holy Light in the Eastweald. It survived Lordaeron's fall and now shelters those in a blighted land. Among the survivors, zealous extremists broke away to form the Scarlet Crusade. More temperate knights and priests joined to establish the Argent Dawn, which chose the hallowed chapel as its forward base.\n\nThe order opens its doors to every race and faction. Alliance and Horde fighters stand together there, seeking to purge the Scourge and reclaim the northern lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Alliance and Horde working together at Light's Hope Chapel?",a="The Argent Dawn sees the Scourge as a threat to every living being, beyond the bitter politics between the Alliance and Horde. Unlike the fanatical, human-supremacist Scarlet Crusade, the Dawn welcomes capable warriors, shamans, druids, and priests of any people willing to fight the undead.",al={"why is horde allowed here","argent dawn neutral","cross faction base"}},{q="Who leads the defenders here?",a="Lord Maxwell Tyrosus leads the Argent Dawn from Light's Hope Chapel. He directs the order's war against the Scourge across the Plaguelands.",al={"who is in charge of lights hope","argent dawn leader","lord tyrosus"}},{q="Why is this chapel so sacred?",a="Light's Hope Chapel is a hallowed chapel of the Church of the Holy Light in the Eastweald. Its sacred ground now shelters the Argent Dawn's headquarters, a rare beacon of the Light deep in the Scourge-held Plaguelands.",al={"what is under the chapel","why does the scourge want lights hope","sanctum beneath chapel"}},{q="What relationship does the chapel have with the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Argent Dawn formed from paladins and priests who rejected the Scarlet Crusade's unhinged zealotry and isolationism. Both orders share the Scourge as an enemy, but the Dawn fights from Light's Hope Chapel on its own terms and welcomes all who would oppose the undead.",al={"are they friends with scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade lights hope","argent dawn vs scarlet crusade"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a holy warrior, you can look to Light's Hope Chapel as a sacred beacon amid death. The Argent Dawn holds this ancient chapel of the Light.",["faction:Horde"]="Though Light's Hope Chapel lies deep in human territory and is run by former Silver Hand knights, Horde fighters are welcome if they prove their dedication to eradicating the undead."},kw={"argent dawn","consecrated ground","eastweald","holy light","lights hope","plaguelands","tyrosus"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:easternplaguelands","npc:lord-maxwell-tyrosus","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:stratholme","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand"},src={"Light's Hope Chapel"}}
E["subzone:marris-stead"] = {t="subzone",n="Marris Stead",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the southwestern Eastern Plaguelands, Nathanos Blightcaller holds Marris Stead. Once a peaceful Lordaeron homestead, the ridge now shelters his lonely, heavily defended redoubt.",h="In the southwestern Eastern Plaguelands, Nathanos Blightcaller holds Marris Stead.",sec={{t="A Ranger's Ruined Home",b="Nathanos Marris once lived at Marris Stead. Before the Third War, the renowned human marksman became the only human ranger lord admitted into the Farstriders. After Stratholme fell, the Scourge swept through Lordaeron. Ramstein the Gorger cornered and killed Nathanos at his own home. The Lich King raised him as a mindless thrall, until Sylvanas Windrunner freed him. Nathanos then joined the Forsaken.",sp=1},{t="The Champion's Bastion",b="Nathanos Blightcaller returned to his ancestral farmstead with his pack of vicious blighthounds. Following the Banshee Queen's orders, he directs strikes across the Plaguelands against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade. Stormwind's intelligence service also turned its attention to the farm. SI:7 operatives sent to investigate Forsaken activity there were slaughtered. The Alliance learned Nathanos had become undead and placed a heavy bounty on his head.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives at Marris Stead?",a="Nathanos Blightcaller lives at Marris Stead with his pack of blighthounds. As Champion of the Banshee Queen, he commands on the front lines.",al={"who is at marris stead","who lives here","npc at farm","nathanos location"}},{q="How did Nathanos become undead?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge devastated Lordaeron and raised many victims as undead. Nathanos's own history and release from Scourge control are told in the protected section.",al={"how did nathanos die","nathanos death","who killed nathanos"}},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in this farm?",a="SI:7 spymaster Mathias Shaw received disturbing reports of unusual Forsaken activity and sent agents to investigate. When only one returned, more investigators went to discover what had happened to the others.",al={"alliance marris stead","si7 plaguelands","why kill nathanos"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="SI:7's missing agents make this Forsaken-held homestead a troubling focus for Alliance investigators in the Plaguelands.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken and their Horde allies, the stead is a heavily defended base for waging war against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"blighthounds","eastern plaguelands","marris stead","nathanos","nathanos blightcaller","nathanos marris","ramstein the gorger","si:7"},rel={"npc:nathanos-blightcaller","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:darrowshire","quest:2300","npc:mathias-shaw"},src={"Marris Stead"}}
E["subzone:northdale"] = {t="subzone",n="Northdale",z="easternplaguelands",s="Northdale lies in ruins north of Light's Hope Chapel, near the border of Quel'Thalas. Banshees, hidden watchers, and corrupted elementals haunt its streets. Here, Taelan Fordring left the Order of the Silver Hand for the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Northdale lies in ruins north of Light's Hope Chapel, near the border of Quel'Thalas.",sec={{t="A Town of Sorrow",b="Northdale lies among the hills north of Light's Hope Chapel, beside the northern highway to Quel'Thalas. The Third War shattered this once peaceful town. Its people were slain or driven away, and its hearths went cold. Now wailing banshees drift among the broken walls. Invisible Eyeless Watchers watch the cursed roads from the dark. The nearby lake has fallen to the plague, too, and corrupted water elementals churn its waters.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Oath",b="After Lordaeron fell and the Knights of the Silver Hand dissolved, young Taelan Fordring stood in Northdale's broken streets. He cast aside his father's teachings. Taelan believed the Silver Hand's remnants were too weak to purge the undead scourge, so he abandoned his sacred duty and joined the radical Scarlet Crusade. His choice shaped the crusade's hold over Hearthglen.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Northdale?",a="The Scourge swept through Lordaeron during the Third War and destroyed Northdale. Its buildings were razed and its people fell to the plague. Now stone ruins remain, haunted by vengeful spirits and corrupted elementals.",al={"why is northdale ruined","northdale history","what is northdale"}},{q="What significant event took place here?",a="In Northdale, Taelan Fordring renounced the Order of the Silver Hand. Despairing over Lordaeron's fall, he cast aside his paladin vows and pledged himself to the emerging Scarlet Crusade.",al={"taelan fordring northdale","what happened to taelan","order of the silver hand northdale"}},{q="What creatures haunt the ruins today?",a="Wailing banshees and unseen Eyeless Watchers serving the Scourge haunt Northdale's ruins. Corrupted water elementals infest the nearby waters.",al={"mobs in northdale","northdale enemies","whats in northdale"}},{q="Where is Northdale located?",a="Northdale lies in the northeastern Eastern Plaguelands, north of Light's Hope Chapel and southeast of the Thalassian Pass into Quel'Thalas.",al={"northdale location","where is northdale","finding northdale"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you stand on the soil where Taelan Fordring abandoned the Silver Hand to pursue vengeance. Northdale is a solemn reminder of lost faith.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you see Northdale's burnt foundations and wandering banshees. They mark another Lordaeron community slaughtered and claimed by the Scourge."},kw={"banshee","eyeless watcher","fordring","northdale","plaguelands","scarlet crusade","silver hand","taelan"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:light"},src={"Northdale"}}
E["subzone:northpass-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Northpass Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Northpass Tower watches over the northern road to Quel'Thalas as a ruin. Shattered during the Third War, the old Lordaeron scout tower still looks toward the elven lands.",h="Northpass Tower watches over the northern road to Quel'Thalas as a ruin.",sec={{t="Northern Sentinel",b="Northpass Tower once guarded Lordaeron's road north into Quel'Thalas. During the Scourge invasion, the tower was reduced to a broken shell. From its high ground, it still overlooks the frontier between Stratholme's blighted outskirts and the distant elven lands.",sp=0},{t="A Silent Watch",b="No garrison mans Northpass Tower today. Its broken walls stand beside the road, now haunted by the Scourge. The ruin marks the watch Lordaeron once kept over the route to Quel'Thalas.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Northpass Tower originally built for?",a="The Kingdom of Lordaeron built Northpass Tower as an observation post to watch the northern road toward Quel'Thalas.",al={"what is northpass tower","northpass history","why was northpass tower built"}},{q="Why is Northpass Tower in ruins?",a="The Scourge destroyed Northpass Tower with Lordaeron's northern defenses during the Third War. Cracked masonry and scaffolding remain.",al={"who destroyed northpass tower","why is northpass tower broken"}},{q="Does anyone hold Northpass Tower now?",a="No one holds Northpass Tower now. The Scourge destroyed it with Lordaeron's northern defenses, leaving an empty ruin along the road north.",al={"why fight over northpass","who controls northpass tower"}},{q="Where does the road past Northpass Tower lead?",a="The road past Northpass Tower heads north toward the Thalassian border and the southern territory of Quel'Thalas.",al={"road past northpass tower","where does northern road go"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see one of Lordaeron's fallen bastions in Northpass Tower, a broken sentinel on the road to the elven lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see in ruins like Northpass Tower how thoroughly the Scourge broke the northern kingdoms' defenses."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","northpass tower","quel'thalas","scourge","scout tower"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:crown-guard-tower","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:thondroril-river","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde"},src={"Northpass Tower"}}
E["subzone:noxious-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Noxious Glade",z="easternplaguelands",s="North of Light's Hope Chapel, the Noxious Glade lies under a heavy veil of plague. The Scourge hold the hollow close to the Argent Dawn's watch.",h="North of Light's Hope Chapel, the Noxious Glade lies under a heavy veil of plague.",sec={{t="A Foul Foothold",b="At Light's Hope Chapel, the Argent Dawn keeps watch while a Scourge camp lies in the hills just north. Plague grips this hollow more fiercely than much of the surrounding land. Sickly green mist fills the air, and the soil has turned a bruised purple.\n\nThe undead have raised ziggurats here, along with a slaughterhouse where they assemble abominations. A plague cauldron continually sends pestilence into the air.",sp=0},{t="Under the Dawn's Gaze",b="The glade lies close enough to Light's Hope Chapel to threaten travelers, couriers, and holy warriors who work from there. Scourge forces build monstrosities and brew toxins in the hollow, hidden from view by the natural ridge.\n\nClimb the path unwary, and the Scourge may be waiting just ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Noxious Glade located?",a="The Noxious Glade lies in the hills immediately north of Light's Hope Chapel, in the eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"where is noxious glade","noxious glade location","how to get to noxious glade"}},{q="Why is the air and ground a different color here?",a="The glade is more heavily blighted than the rest of the Plaguelands. A working plague cauldron and nearby Scourge structures send toxins into the hollow, darkening the earth purple and filling the clearing with poisonous green haze.",al={"why is it green","why is ground purple","noxious glade blight"}},{q="What Scourge structures are in the glade?",a="The glade holds several ziggurats, a plague cauldron, and a slaughterhouse where the Scourge assemble monstrous constructs such as abominations.",al={"what is inside noxious glade","noxious glade buildings"}},{q="Does the Argent Dawn know about this place?",a="Yes. The Argent Dawn knows of the glade, but its forces are stretched thin defending against Scourge attacks across the Plaguelands, leaving this nearby outpost dangerous.",al={"lights hope chapel aware","argent dawn noxious glade"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see how close Scourge blight has come to Light's Hope Chapel. Undead abominations and necromancers fill the glade.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead champion, you may recognize these slaughterhouses and plague cauldrons as tools of the Lich King's rule. They show the fate that awaits those who do not break free."},kw={"blight","eastern plaguelands","light's hope chapel","noxious glade","plague cauldron","scourge","slaughterhouse","ziggurat"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:cauldron","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Noxious Glade"}}
E["subzone:pestilent-scar"] = {t="subzone",n="Pestilent Scar",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the Eastern Plaguelands, ravenous oozes churn across the floor of Pestilent Scar. The hollow seems older than the Scourge blight that fills it.",h="In the Eastern Plaguelands, ravenous oozes churn across the floor of Pestilent Scar.",sec={{t="A Blighted Chasm",b="Pestilent Scar cuts through the eastern reaches of the Eastern Plaguelands, a gloomy rift in corrupted land. Nearby, sudden eruptions of the Plague of Undeath tore open Infectis Scar. Pestilent Scar seems to have formed naturally, perhaps as a deep river canyon or a lake that dried when the Scourge swept across Lordaeron. Barren at first, the trench gradually filled with noxious runoff and foul slime.",sp=0},{t="The Slime Pits",b="Without pure water and under constant unholy decay, the hollow now breeds mutated, acidic slimes and carrion vermin. Crossing its crumbling rim is dangerous. Acrid fumes choke the air above the drop, and unstable soil can send the unwary into the churning muck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pestilent Scar?",a="Pestilent Scar is a sunken gorge in the Eastern Plaguelands. Corruption took hold during Lordaeron's fall, leaving foul runoff, diseased soil, and aggressive oozes.",al={"pestilent scar lore","what is pestilent scar","pestilent scar canyon"}},{q="How did the Pestilent Scar form?",a="Unlike fissures torn open by Scourge eruptions, Pestilent Scar seems to have begun as a natural valley, lake, or river canyon. The Plague of Undeath blighted it until it dried and withered.",al={"how was pestilent scar made","pestilent scar origin","who made pestilent scar"}},{q="How does it differ from the Infectis Scar?",a="Infectis Scar was violently ripped open as an unnatural volcanic rupture filled with magical blight. Pestilent Scar seems to be an older natural depression that gradually gathered corruption and runoff after the land died.",al={"pestilent scar vs infectis scar","infectis scar difference"}},{q="What creatures live in the Pestilent Scar?",a="Acidic oozes spawned by the plague and carrion-eating vermin live on the chasm floor, among poisonous pools and rotting organic matter.",al={"pestilent scar mobs","what lives in pestilent scar"}}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Along the gorge's edges, concentrated rot can nurture rare plants hardened by blight, such as Arthas' Tears and Plaguebloom, along the cliffs.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you may know that Forsaken apothecaries study slimes from deep fissures to isolate unstable forms of the Scourge's foulest toxins."},kw={"blight","eastern plaguelands","gorge","infectis scar","oozes","pestilent scar","slime"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:infectis-scar","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Pestilent Scar"}}
E["subzone:plaguewood"] = {t="subzone",n="Plaguewood",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scarlet Crusaders patrol Plaguewood, where the Scourge gathers south of Stratholme. Greenwood has become a blighted forest choked with fungus.",h="Scarlet Crusaders patrol Plaguewood, where the Scourge gathers south of Stratholme.",sec={{t="From Greenwood to Decay",b="Before the Third War, Greenwood was a forest much like Elwynn's lush woods. A modest village stood by its entrance, and farmers and soldiers traveled the roads. Then tainted grain came from Andorhal, and the woodland fell. Rich earth turned to spongy, corrupted soil. Huge mushrooms now dwarf the dead trees and spread noxious brown vapors over the forest floor.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of the Dead",b="The Scourge has taken Plaguewood and made it a staging ground for the undead around Stratholme. Ziggurats and slaughterhouses dot the ruined land, producing abominations and cultists. Scarlet Crusaders patrol the road to Stratholme's gates, bent on purging the Scourge. They also slaughter any living travelers they meet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was this forest called before the plague?",a="Before the Third War, the forest was called Greenwood. A small village stood near its entrance, and its woods resembled Elwynn Forest in beauty and climate.",al={"plaguewood old name","greenwood lore","what was plaguewood"}},{q="Why are there massive mushrooms growing everywhere?",a="The plague warped the forest's soil and growth. Monstrous fungi now rise from the spongy ground and belch noxious brown clouds like those from plague cauldrons.",al={"giant mushrooms plaguewood","fungus plaguewood","why mushrooms"}},{q="Who controls the Plaguewood today?",a="The Scourge holds most of Plaguewood, with necromancers, ghouls, ziggurats, and slaughterhouses. Scarlet Crusader patrols march along the main roads, attacking undead and living travelers on sight.",al={"who rules plaguewood","plaguewood enemies","who lives in plaguewood"}},{q="Where does the road through the woods lead?",a="The main road runs north to the gates of Stratholme. Westward, the blighted woods reach toward the ruined village of Terrordale.",al={"plaguewood road destination","where does path go","stratholme road"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face abominations and unyielding fanatics among Plaguewood's twisted trees and foul cauldrons. The land recalls Lordaeron's fall and tests your devotion to the Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance survivor, you walk the road Prince Arthas took toward the purge of Stratholme. Rot and mad Scarlet zealots line the way."},kw={"fungus","greenwood","plaguewood","scourge","slaughterhouses","stratholme","terrordale","ziggurats"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:terrordale","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","subzone:andorhal","zone:elwynn"},src={"Plaguewood"}}
E["subzone:plaguewood-tower"] = {t="subzone",n="Plaguewood Tower",z="easternplaguelands",s="Plaguewood Tower watches over the northern trails near Terrordale, its stones broken. Lordaeron kept a watchpost here until the Scourge invasion brought it to ruin.",h="Plaguewood Tower watches over the northern trails near Terrordale, its stones broken.",sec={{t="A Ruined Sentinel in the North",b="Plaguewood Tower's fractured stones overlook the northern trails between the Plaguewood and blighted Terrordale. The Kingdom of Lordaeron kept this post to guard the region.\n\nWhen the Scourge swept across the land, the tower was battered into ruins among corrupted fungal canopies. Its broken walls still face the trails, the last remnant of Lordaeron's watch here.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Plaguewood Tower originally used for?",a="The Kingdom of Lordaeron built Plaguewood Tower as a regional watchtower. Before the Third War, guards watched the northern forests, roads and settlements such as Terrordale from here. The Scourge overwhelmed and shattered the garrison.",al={"original purpose","who built plaguewood tower","history of tower"}},{q="Where exactly is the tower located?",a="Plaguewood Tower stands in the northern Eastern Plaguelands, within the Plaguewood, just outside ruined Terrordale and south of Stratholme's outer blighted reaches.",al={"tower location","where is plaguewood tower","map location"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Lordaeron's shattered watchtowers recall the human lands lost to the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, ruined fortifications like Plaguewood Tower show how thoroughly the Scourge broke the northern kingdoms' defenses."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","outpost","plaguewood","plaguewood tower","scourge","terrordale","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:plaguewood","subzone:terrordale","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge","topic:alliance","topic:horde","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Plaguewood Tower"}}
E["subzone:quel-lithien-lodge"] = {t="subzone",n="Quel'Lithien Lodge",z="easternplaguelands",s="Farstrider rangers keep watch at Quel'Lithien Lodge, amid the blighted woods of the Eastern Plaguelands. The high elven hunting lodge stands among the northern hills near the entrance to Quel'Thalas. The Scourge surround it, and Forsaken agents hunt its rangers as they guard old elven archives.",h="Farstrider rangers keep watch at Quel'Lithien Lodge, amid the blighted woods of the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Ranger Camp in the Blight",b="Before the Third War, Farstriders kept camp at Quel'Lithien on the road to Quel'Thalas. The lodge held records of the ranger order. Then the Scourge swept through Lordaeron and into the elven kingdom, and the lodge's fortunes worsened. Now its rangers watch over the corrupted forest. They are one of only two major concentrations of high elves left in Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Hunted in the Plaguelands",b="Nathanos Blightcaller has sent Horde champions to infiltrate Quel'Lithien Lodge. Once a solitary human Ranger Lord, he trained alongside these very elves. He seeks the Quel'Thalas Registry, an official record of the ranger order and elven lineages. Nathanos has ordered the lodge's defenders slaughtered so the record can be taken. The rangers face a siege from former allies and the undead around them.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why are there living high elves in the Eastern Plaguelands?",a="Quel'Lithien has long been a Farstrider camp. Its high elven rangers remain here after the Scourge laid waste to the region. They hold one of Lordaeron's last elven footholds near the road to Quel'Thalas.",al={"why high elves here","who lives at quel'lithien","quellithien elves"}},{q="Are the elves at Quel'Lithien Lodge part of the Alliance?",a="No. The lodge welcomes Alliance travelers and is openly hostile toward the Horde. Yet it is an autonomous high elven settlement, without formal support or direction from Stormwind or Ironforge.",al={"are quellithien elves alliance","quellithien faction"}},{q="Why does Nathanos Blightcaller target the lodge?",a="Nathanos Blightcaller sends Horde agents to seize the Quel'Thalas Registry. The lodge's archives hold this important historical record of elven ranger personnel and lineages.",al={"why nathanos attack quellithien","the ranger lord's behest","quel'thalas registry"}},{q="How does Quel'Lithien differ from Quel'Danil Lodge?",a="Both were historic high elven hunting lodges. Quel'Danil lies among friendly Wildhammer dwarves in the Hinterlands. Quel'Lithien stands isolated in the Eastern Plaguelands, between blighted ruins and the closed gates of Quel'Thalas.",al={"queldanil vs quellithien","hinterlands lodge comparison"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see Farstriders carrying centuries of classical Thalassian marksmanship. They rely on those survival skills in a hostile wilderness, cut off from civil society.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are sent here from Marris Stead on Nathanos Blightcaller's orders. You are to seize high elven records by force."},kw={"farstrider","high elves","marris stead","quel'lithien","quel'thalas registry","quellithien"},rel={"npc:nathanos-blightcaller","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:alliance","topic:horde","topic:third-war"},src={"Quel'Lithien Lodge"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-base-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Base Camp",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scarlet forces hold a barricaded camp on Lake Mereldar’s eastern shore, just west of Tyr’s Hand. It marks an outer line of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Scarlet forces hold a barricaded camp on Lake Mereldar’s eastern shore, just west of Tyr’s Hand.",sec={{t="A Forward Line on Lake Mereldar",b="On Lake Mereldar’s eastern shore, just west of Tyr’s Hand, the Scarlet Crusade holds a barricaded camp. It guards an outer line in the blighted countryside.",sp=0},{t="Shielding the Bastion",b="Tyr’s Hand is one of the Scarlet Crusade’s strongholds in Lordaeron. Scarlet Base Camp guards its western approaches as the Crusade seeks to reclaim land from the undead. Outsiders are met with suspicion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Scarlet Base Camp?",a="Scarlet Base Camp is a barricaded Scarlet Crusade position on Lake Mereldar’s eastern shore, just west of Tyr’s Hand.",al={"what is scarlet base camp","why is scarlet camp here","purpose of base camp"}},{q="Who leads the forces stationed at the camp?",a="No commander is identified for the original Classic camp. The Scarlet Crusade holds the position near Tyr’s Hand.",al={"who leads scarlet base camp","camp commander","scarlet camp leaders"}},{q="Are the occupants hostile to travelers?",a="The Scarlet Crusade treats outsiders of both factions as possible plague carriers or agents of the Scourge, and is hostile to them.",al={"will scarlet base camp attack me","is scarlet camp hostile","are they friendly"}},{q="Where is the camp in relation to Lake Mereldar?",a="Scarlet Base Camp lies on Lake Mereldar’s eastern shore, just west of Tyr’s Hand.",al={"scarlet base camp lake","where is scarlet camp","camp near tyrs hand"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see the Silver Hand’s legacy corrupted. Zeal to defend Lordaeron’s holy ground has turned into aggressive suspicion of fellow survivors.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you face living zealots who seek to purge the Forsaken from Lordaeron as ruthlessly as they hunt the mindless Scourge."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","lake mereldar","scarlet base camp","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:lake-mereldar","subzone:tyr-s-hand","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Scarlet Base Camp"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-basilica"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Basilica",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Tyr's Hand, Scarlet Basilica commands the Scarlet Crusade's eastern forces. Crusader Lord Valdelmar oversees the cathedral, a stronghold against the Scourge in the Eastern Plaguelands.",h="At Tyr's Hand, Scarlet Basilica commands the Scarlet Crusade's eastern forces.",sec={{t="Heart of the Eastern Crusade",b="At Tyr's Hand, Scarlet Basilica rises above the Eastern Plaguelands as the Scarlet Crusade's cathedral and command center. The Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades remains the order's spiritual heart, while the basilica anchors its surviving stronghold in Lordaeron. Elite crusaders guard its walls. Inside, Crusader Lord Valdelmar directs the local defense and drives away outsiders who approach.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scarlet Basilica?",a="Scarlet Basilica is the Scarlet Crusade's grand cathedral at Tyr's Hand in the Eastern Plaguelands. It is the order's eastern seat of religious and military authority.",al={"scarlet basilica info","what is this cathedral","tyrs hand church"}},{q="Who leads the forces inside the Basilica?",a="Crusader Lord Valdelmar commands the forces inside Scarlet Basilica. He is a high-ranking Scarlet Crusade leader who holds Tyr's Hand against the Scourge and other enemies he perceives.",al={"who is in scarlet basilica","valdelmar","scarlet basilica boss"}},{q="How does this compare to the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades is the Scarlet Crusade's primary spiritual headquarters. Scarlet Basilica is its eastern counterpart, a fortified religious center in the Plaguelands.",al={"monastery vs basilica","is this the scarlet monastery"}},{q="Are travelers welcome inside the Basilica?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade attacks travelers who do not wear its crimson colors, believing them tainted by undeath. Alliance and Horde intruders are attacked on sight.",al={"can alliance enter","is scarlet basilica hostile","can i visit"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see holy devotion twisted into merciless fanaticism at Scarlet Basilica. Former knights of the Silver Hand serve there.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you face one of the zealots' most entrenched outposts. The Scarlet Crusade seeks to eradicate all undead, regardless of free will."},kw={"cathedral","crusader lord valdelmar","eastern plaguelands","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","subzone:high-seat","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Basilica"}}
E["subzone:stratholme"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scourge forces hold Stratholme, and its ruins still burn. Once the jewel of the Eastweald and Lordaeron’s second greatest city, it became the place where Prince Arthas Menethil ordered the culling of citizens who had eaten grain tainted by the Plague of Undeath.",h="Scourge forces hold Stratholme, and its ruins still burn.",sec={{t="Cradle of Paladins and Trade",b="Stratholme rose with the Arathi expansion into the Eastweald centuries ago. It became Lordaeron’s second-largest settlement, famed for holy shrines and sacred water that resisted dark sorcery. Before the Second War, Archbishop Alonsus Faol gathered at the city’s chapel and founded the Order of the Knights of the Silver Hand.\n\nAmong its first legends was Uther the Lightbringer. During the Second War, Stratholme served the Alliance of Lordaeron as a vital port, supply hub, and northern oil refinery. The Old Horde assaulted it, but victory brought the city’s rebuilding.",sp=0},{t="The Culling and Eternal Ruin",b="The Cult of the Damned carried infected grain from Andorhal into Stratholme’s markets. Unaware of the taint, thousands ate the flour. Prince Arthas arrived with Uther and Jaina Proudmoore, but the infection had spread too far to cure.\n\nHe judged slaughter the only way to deny Mal'Ganis an entire army and ordered every citizen killed. The atrocity drove Uther and Jaina away and began the prince’s descent into madness. His forces set the city ablaze. Then the Scourge took its smoking ruins for their regional capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stratholme still burning?",a="During the Third War, Prince Arthas’s forces set Stratholme’s homes and streets ablaze to kill the infected and halt the spread of undeath. The plague-tainted fire has burned ever since, fed by dark necromantic energies and the Scourge infestation.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","fire in stratholme","stratholme smoke"}},{q="What was the Culling of Stratholme?",a="The Culling of Stratholme was Prince Arthas Menethil’s slaughter of the city’s people. After they ate grain infected with the Plague of Undeath, he ordered every inhabitant killed, sick or healthy, before they could rise as Scourge soldiers. His choice broke his alliances and his moral compass.",al={"the culling","arthas purge","purge of stratholme"}},{q="What historic role did Stratholme play for the Silver Hand?",a="Archbishop Alonsus Faol founded the Knights of the Silver Hand in Stratholme’s Alonsus Chapel before the Second War. He anointed its first five members, including Uther the Lightbringer, Turalyon, and Saidan Dathrohan.",al={"silver hand origin","alonsus chapel","order of the silver hand stratholme"}},{q="What happened to Tirion Fordring here?",a="Years after the Second War, Lord Tirion Fordring stood trial for treason in Stratholme’s Hall of Justice after defending the honorable orc hermit Eitrigg. Uther and Alliance leaders judged him, stripped him of his title, and exiled him. Tirion later freed Eitrigg during an attack on the city led by Thrall.",al={"tirion fordring trial","tirion trial stratholme","eitrigg trial"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can look to Stratholme as hallowed ground turned tragic. The Order of the Silver Hand began here, and Arthas shattered that brotherhood when he demanded the slaughter of innocent citizens.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you see a ruined city that recalls Lordaeron’s fall and the heavy price the northern kingdoms paid to plague and treachery."},kw={"andorhal","arthas","culling","eastweald","mal'ganis","plaguelands","scourge","silver hand","stratholme","uther"},rel={"topic:arthas-menethil","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","subzone:andorhal","npc:tirion-fordring","topic:lordaeron","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Stratholme"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-classic"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme (Classic)",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scourge and Scarlet Crusade forces fight through Stratholme's burning ruins. Once northern Lordaeron's jewel and the birthplace of the Silver Hand, the city now lies divided between them.",h="Scourge and Scarlet Crusade forces fight through Stratholme's burning ruins.",sec={{t="The Cursed Capital",b="Stratholme once held great power in northern Lordaeron and gave birth to the Knights of the Silver Hand. During the Third War, Prince Arthas purged the city after infected grain carried plague through its gates. He slaughtered his own subjects. The city smoldered in ruins, then the Scourge claimed it.\n\nKel'Thuzad holds overarching authority, while Baron Rivendare commands the undead forces in the field. From Stratholme, they direct Scourge power across the Plaguelands.",sp=0},{t="A Divided Warfront",b="Two vicious factions wage an unending war through Stratholme. In the west, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade holds Crusaders' Square and the Scarlet Bastion under Grand Crusader Saidan Dathrohan. In the east, Scourge slaughterhouses and necropolises stand behind towering ziggurats. The death knight Baron Rivendare guards them.\n\nBurning tenements and restless spirits surround anyone who enters. Across the city, both sides trade blows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Stratholme still burning?",a="Prince Arthas set Stratholme ablaze during his purge in the Third War, hoping to stop the plague of undeath from spreading. Dark magic, necromancy, and the unending war between the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade keep the fires smoldering.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","who burned stratholme","stratholme burning"}},{q="Who controls Stratholme right now?",a="Control is divided between the Scarlet Crusade in the west and the Scourge in the east. Grand Crusader Dathrohan leads the Crusaders from their western bastion. Baron Rivendare rules the eastern ruins for the Scourge under Kel'Thuzad.",al={"who rules stratholme","who is in charge of stratholme","stratholme leaders"}},{q="What is the historical significance of the city to paladins?",a="Stratholme gave birth to the Order of the Silver Hand. There, Archbishop Alonsus Faol first consecrated Uther the Lightbringer and the original paladins. The city's fall marks the deepest tragedy in the order's history.",al={"silver hand stratholme","paladin history stratholme"}},{q="How do you enter the Scourge-controlled side of the city?",a="You can fight through the main gate to reach the eastern Scourge district, or enter directly through the Service Entrance. Magistrate Barthilas holds the key to that back gate. Skilled rogues, powerful blacksmith skeleton keys, or goblin explosives can breach it.",al={"back door key","service entrance stratholme","how to get into undead side"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, Stratholme's desecration cuts deeply. It is the sacred birthplace of the Silver Hand and the graveyard where Arthas shattered Uther's guidance.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier or survivor, Stratholme recalls Lordaeron's catastrophic fall and the terrible cost of the Third War."},kw={"arthas","dathrohan","plaguelands","purge","rivendare","silver hand","slaughterhouse","stratholme"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lich-king","topic:light"},src={"Stratholme (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-main-gate"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme Main Gate",z="easternplaguelands",s="Ruined avenues beyond Stratholme Main Gate lead toward King’s Square and the Scarlet Bastion. The gate stands in the northwestern Eastern Plaguelands, at the entrance to Lordaeron’s northern metropolis.",h="Ruined avenues beyond Stratholme Main Gate lead toward King’s Square and the Scarlet Bastion.",sec={{t="Gateway to a Fallen Jewel",b="Stratholme was once northern Lordaeron’s pride and the birthplace of the Order of the Silver Hand. Its great arched gates now mark the edge of a nightmare begun during the Third War. Here, Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther the Lightbringer. He purged his own citizens before the Plague of Undeath could claim them. The city has burned ever since and is now the region’s chief Scourge stronghold.",sp=0},{t="The Scarlet Approach",b="Beyond the main gate, the road passes through the ruins of King’s Square and Market Row toward the fortified Scarlet Bastion. Scarlet Crusade zealots entered here to reclaim the city and purge the dead, then made an encampment in the ruins. Overwhelming undead surround them. The crusaders fight an attrition war against the dark forces directing Stratholme’s defense, and they cannot win.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this gate lead?",a="The main gate opens into King’s Square and Market Row. From there, the route continues toward the Scarlet Bastion, where the Scarlet Crusade contests the district.",al={"where does strat main gate go","what is stratholme main gate","front entrance strat"}},{q="Why is the city behind these gates still burning?",a="During the Third War, Prince Arthas purged the city and set it ablaze to stop the Plague of Undeath from spreading. Dark necromantic magic, unholy fires, and Scourge corruption have kept the ruins burning without pause ever since.",al={"why is stratholme on fire","who burned stratholme","fire in stratholme"}},{q="What is the difference between this gate and the Service Entrance?",a="Both gates enter the same vast ruined city from opposite ends. The Main Gate opens near the city’s living and Scarlet-held quarters. The Service Entrance opens onto eastern streets beneath the Scourge slaughterhouses and Baron Rivendare’s rule.",al={"main gate vs service entrance","which strat entrance","strat doors"}},{q="Who controls the area immediately inside the Main Gate?",a="Zombies, ghouls, skeletal horrors, and wandering shades prowl the first streets beyond the archway. Farther along the avenues, the Scarlet Crusade holds an embattled bastion.",al={"who is inside main gate","what mobs are at strat front"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you may grieve at these gates. Here, on the day he purged Stratholme, Arthas disbanded the Silver Hand and fractured the order.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you pass beneath an archway that once marked the grand entrance to Lordaeron’s second-greatest capital. The city behind it is now an ash-choked necropolis."},kw={"arthas","eastern plaguelands","front entrance","king's square","main gate","scarlet bastion","scourge","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","subzone:stratholme-service-entrance","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","topic:lordaeron","topic:third-war","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Stratholme Main Gate"}}
E["subzone:stratholme-service-entrance"] = {t="subzone",n="Stratholme Service Entrance",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Eastwall Gate in the northern Eastern Plaguelands, the Scourge holds Stratholme's eastern quarter. The Service Entrance cuts through the city's fortified wall.",h="At Eastwall Gate in the northern Eastern Plaguelands, the Scourge holds Stratholme's eastern quarter.",sec={{t="A Breached Bastion",b="Stratholme's Main Gate opens into King's Square, with a road toward the Scarlet Bastion. At Eastwall Gate, the Service Entrance breaks through the eastern fortification. Beyond it lie Elders' Square and blighted paths to Baron Rivendare's slaughterhouses.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge Redoubt",b="The Service Entrance gives a shorter way into Stratholme's eastern districts. The Scourge holds the alleys and ziggurats, guarded by gargoyles, crypt fiends, and cultists. The Argent Dawn and bold adventurers gather here before striking at the Lich King's commanders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Stratholme Service Entrance located?",a="The entrance lies at Eastwall Gate, along the northern mountains of the Eastern Plaguelands, just east of Stratholme's main ruins. A stone archway cuts into the fortified wall there.",al={"service entrance location","where is back gate","strat side entrance map","how to find strat back door"}},{q="How does this entrance differ from the Stratholme Main Gate?",a="The Main Gate opens into King's Square and leads across the city toward the Scarlet Bastion. The Service Entrance opens near Elders' Square, closer to the undead-held eastern districts and Slaughter Square.",al={"back door vs front door","service entrance difference","which strat entrance"}},{q="Why is it called the Service Entrance?",a="The reason for the name Service Entrance is not given.",al={"why service entrance","service gate lore"}},{q="Who controls this part of the city?",a="The Scourge controls the district beyond the gate. Baron Rivendare and his acolytes oversee it and maintain the ziggurats that anchor their dark magic within Elders' Square.",al={"who controls back gate","service entrance bosses","undead side leader"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you enter the Scourge's defiled necromantic apparatus. The gate gives you a direct path to purge Rivendare and reclaim the holy city's fallen honor.",["class:Rogue"]="As a rogue, you can use the service gate to slip around fortified battle lines and enter the city's utility corridors."},kw={"back door","baron rivendare","eastern plaguelands","eastwall gate","elders square","scourge","service entrance","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:stratholme","subzone:eastwall-gate","subzone:stratholme-main-gate","zone:easternplaguelands","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Stratholme Service Entrance"}}
E["subzone:terrordale"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrordale",z="easternplaguelands",s="Terrordale’s streets lie in ruin beneath restless dead, beside Plaguewood and Terrorweb Tunnel. In the northwestern Eastern Plaguelands, Scourge horrors and tormented spirits haunt what remains.",h="Terrordale’s streets lie in ruin beneath restless dead, beside Plaguewood and Terrorweb Tunnel.",sec={{t="A Haunted Haven on the Wood's Edge",b="Terrordale fell to the Scourge with the rest of Lordaeron. Near Terrorweb Tunnel’s mouth, restless shades and wandering undead fill the ruined village streets. Plaguewood’s trees press against its rotting timber. A few eccentric residents still dare to stay. Augustus the Touched is a peculiar merchant, while Egan hunts ghosts and seeks to free the tortured spirits caught between worlds.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Disturbance and Exorcism",b="Terrordale’s spirits remain in agony, bound to the earth by their tragic ends. Their anguish disturbs the spirit realm so deeply that the physical world buckles beneath it. Seasoned paladins come under the guidance of the Silver Hand and Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker. Through rites of judgment and sacrifice, they seek to banish the torment. The work tests their holy discipline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Terrordale?",a="Terrordale lies in the northwestern Eastern Plaguelands, a ruined hamlet west of Plaguewood and south of Terrorweb Tunnel. Scourge horrors and tormented ghosts overrun it.",al={"where is terrordale","what is this town","terrordale lore"}},{q="Who are the people still in the town?",a="Two eccentric figures linger among Terrordale’s ruins. Egan hunts ghosts and tries to pacify and free the trapped spirits. Augustus the Touched is a half-mad undead hermit and merchant, intent on recovering his old ledgers and possessions.",al={"who is egan","who is augustus","living npcs in terrordale"}},{q="What connects this town to the paladin trials?",a="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sends paladins seeking to bond with their holy warhorse charger to Terrordale. They use an exorcism censer to banish the tormented spirits. The trial proves the spiritual resolve, judgment, and sacrifice required of an elite knight of the Light.",al={"paladin charger terrordale","exorcising terrordale","lord grayson shadowbreaker"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you face a trial in Terrordale. Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker sends candidates for the charger steed into the ruined hamlet to exorcise its weeping spirits.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Terrordale’s broken houses recall the fall of northern Lordaeron. Common citizens’ spirits remain trapped in death in their own front yards."},kw={"augustus the touched","charger","eastern plaguelands","egan","grayson shadowbreaker","plaguewood","terrordale","terrorweb tunnel"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:plaguewood","subzone:terrorweb-tunnel","npc:lord-grayson-shadowbreaker","subzone:thondroril-river","subzone:northdale","topic:scourge","subzone:darkshire"},src={"Terrordale"}}
E["subzone:terrorweb-tunnel"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrorweb Tunnel",z="easternplaguelands",s="Crypt fiends swarm through Terrorweb Tunnel, the mountain way between Terrordale and the Thondroril River.",h="Crypt fiends swarm through Terrorweb Tunnel, the mountain way between Terrordale and the Thondroril River.",sec={{t="A Subterranean Infestation",b="Terrorweb Tunnel cuts through the mountains beside the Thondroril River. It runs from Terrordale to the riverbanks south of the village. Crypt fiends fill the passage where ghouls or skeletal sentries might be found. These mummified nerubian arachnids were raised to serve the Lich King. The tunnel shortens the route around the mountain slopes, but thick webs and towering Nerubian Overseers make the dark way dangerous to cross.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Terrorweb Tunnel lead?",a="Terrorweb Tunnel cuts through the mountain range northwest of Terrordale. Its northern entrance opens into Terrordale, and its southern mouth reaches the rocky banks overlooking the Thondroril River.",al={"terrorweb tunnel path","where does terrorweb go","terrorweb connections"}},{q="What creatures inhabit the tunnel?",a="Crypt fiends swarm through Terrorweb Tunnel. These undead nerubian spider-lords came from ancient Northrend. Formidable Nerubian Overseers also stalk the passages, making travel dangerous.",al={"terrorweb mobs","who lives in terrorweb tunnel","terrorweb tunnel monsters"}},{q="Who is nearby outside the tunnel?",a="The exiled paladin Tirion Fordring keeps a modest campsite along the Thondroril River, near Terrorweb Tunnel’s southern mouth.",al={"who is outside terrorweb","tirion near terrorweb","npc near terrorweb tunnel"}},{q="Why are nerubians in the Plaguelands?",a="The Lich King conquered Azjol-Nerub, the subterranean kingdom in Northrend, and reanimated fallen nerubians as crypt fiends. When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, these arachnid shock troops went south to enforce the Cult of the Damned’s grip on the region.",al={"why crypt fiends here","nerubians in plaguelands"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can find the exiled Tirion Fordring near Terrorweb Tunnel’s southern mouth. He keeps a modest campsite along the Thondroril River."},kw={"crypt fiends","nerubian","nerubian overseer","terrordale","terrorweb tunnel","thondroril river","tirion fordring"},rel={"subzone:terrordale","subzone:thondroril-river","npc:tirion-fordring","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Terrorweb Tunnel"}}
E["subzone:thondroril-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Thondroril River",z="easternplaguelands",s="At Thondroril River, plague taints the waters between the Western and Eastern Plaguelands. It rises near Terrorweb Tunnel in Northern Lordaeron and flows south into Darrowmere Lake. Once a route for trade and travel through the fallen kingdom, its banks now shelter monstrous Scourge beasts and a legendary hermit.",h="At Thondroril River, plague taints the waters between the Western and Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A River Cut by Ruin",b="Before Lordaeron fell, traffic followed Thondroril north toward the kingdom's holdings and south to Darrowmere Lake. Now the river marks a dangerous divide between the Western and Eastern Plaguelands.\n\nPlague taints the water. Giant maggots, plaguebats, diseased bears, and predatory snapjaws infest the banks. Where a scenic riverbed once offered passage, travelers now face a deadly crossing.",sp=0},{t="Watchers on the Bank",b="Tirion Fordring lives on the eastern bank in an overgrown homestead. The exiled Paladin lost his titles and went into hiding years ago.\n\nFrom that refuge, the former lord watches the rotting river and the ruin of his homeland. He tests the mettle and conscience of adventurers who cross the blighted frontier.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Thondroril River begin and end?",a="Thondroril River rises in Northern Lordaeron near the entrance to Terrorweb Tunnel. It flows south across the Plaguelands into Darrowmere Lake, then continues south beyond the lake as the Darrowmere River.",al={"thondroril river path","where does thondroril flow","source of thondroril"}},{q="What dangerous creatures live along the riverbanks?",a="Giant maggots, diseased bears, plaguebats, crypt spiders, and river snapjaws stalk the banks. Plague has turned native wildlife into lethal creatures.",al={"monsters near river","thondroril mobs","river threats"}},{q="Who is the old man living by the eastern shore?",a="Tirion Fordring lives in a dilapidated farmhouse on the eastern bank. He was one of the original Knights of the Silver Hand, and the Alliance exiled him years before the Third War. Now he lives in seclusion, watching the Scourge.",al={"who is by the river","old hermit thondroril","thondroril questgiver"}},{q="Why does the river divide the two Plaguelands?",a="Thondroril River forms a wide natural gorge through central Lordaeron. After the Scourge brought down the kingdom, cartographers and survivors came to treat the river as the frontier between the Western and Eastern Plaguelands.",al={"western vs eastern border","plaguelands boundary"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a Paladin, you can find Tirion Fordring on the river's eastern shore. He helped found the Silver Hand, and his legacy endures despite his exile.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Along the damp, rotting riverbed, you can find hardy plague-tainted plants such as Sungrass, Arthas' Tears, and Plaguebloom near the murky shores."},kw={"darrowmere lake","eastern plaguelands","lordaeron","terrorweb tunnel","thondroril","thondroril river","tirion fordring","western plaguelands"},rel={"npc:tirion-fordring","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:darrowmere-lake","subzone:terrorweb-tunnel","subzone:stratholme","topic:lordaeron","topic:second-war"},src={"Thondroril River"}}
E["subzone:tyr-s-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Tyr's Hand",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the southeastern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, Scarlet Crusaders hold Tyr's Hand as their chief stronghold and supply hub. The city was once sacred to the Church of the Holy Light, and its walls remain heavily fortified.",h="In the southeastern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, Scarlet Crusaders hold Tyr's Hand as their chief...",sec={{t="A City of Churches",b="Tyr's Hand rises from the old Eastweald, once a green land in Lordaeron, as one of humanity's most ancient sacred sites. Shrines and holy buildings stand across its grounds, giving it the name “city of churches.” The land around it has rotted under blight, yet Tyr's Hand remains remarkably preserved behind thick walls and formidable stonework. The Scarlet Basilica towers above the city.",sp=0},{t="Fortress of the Scarlet Crusade",b="Lord Valdelmar kept Tyr's Hand standing through military vigilance and faith as the Scourge swept through Lordaeron during the Third War. After the Knights of the Silver Hand split into rival factions, Tyr's Hand joined the Crimson dawn of the Scarlet Crusade. High General Brigitte Abbendis and Valdelmar lead the city from its impenetrable base.\n\nElite crusaders train in the abbey. Heavily guarded couriers keep contact with Scarlet forces holding Stratholme, while the city ruthlessly rebuffs outsiders at its gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the city called Tyr's Hand?",a="The name Tyr's Hand is ancient, and surviving records from Lordaeron say little about who Tyr was. The site is one of the oldest and most revered holy places of the Church of the Holy Light in the old Eastweald.",al={"who is tyr","tyrs hand name meaning","origin of tyrs hand"}},{q="Why hasn't the Scourge overrun Tyr's Hand?",a="Tyr's Hand guards a natural mountain chokepoint with formidable stone fortifications, barracks, and an abbey. The Scarlet Crusade keeps an elite, heavily armed garrison there, whose martial zeal and radiant holy magic have repelled relentless Scourge assaults.",al={"why did tyrs hand survive","how is tyrs hand not undead","how does tyrs hand hold out"}},{q="Are travelers and adventurers welcome in Tyr's Hand?",a="No. The Scarlet Crusade has fallen into xenophobic paranoia and sees anyone outside its ranks as a possible carrier of the undead plague or a secret Scourge agent. Outsiders are attacked on sight.",al={"can i visit tyrs hand","is tyrs hand friendly","are scarlet crusaders friendly here"}},{q="What role did the city play during the Second War?",a="During the Second War, Alterac provocateurs secretly stirred a peasant revolt in Tyr's Hand to conceal a nearby orcish mining outpost. After the Alliance and the Silver Hand subdued the unrest, Horde ogre magi heavily bombarded the city and sacked the neighboring bay to cut Quel'Thalas supply lines.",al={"second war tyrs hand","peasant revolt tyrs hand"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors, Tyr's Hand shows how an ancient cradle of the Silver Hand can be twisted into a bastion of unyielding Scarlet zealotry when faith loses compassion.",["class:Priest"]="The abbey and Scarlet Basilica are magnificent works of early Church of the Holy Light architecture, though their clergy have traded pastoral healing for blind crusade."},kw={"abbendis","demetria","eastweald","holy light","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand","valdelmar"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-basilica","subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:church-of-the-holy-light","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","zone:easternplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","topic:scourge"},src={"Tyr's Hand"}}
E["subzone:tyr-s-hand-abbey"] = {t="subzone",n="Tyr's Hand Abbey",z="easternplaguelands",s="In Tyr's Hand, the Scarlet Crusade keeps the abbey for worship and study. The fortified city stands in the southeastern Eastern Plaguelands, where the abbey supports the grand Scarlet Basilica.",h="In Tyr's Hand, the Scarlet Crusade keeps the abbey for worship and study.",sec={{t="Sanctuary of the Zealots",b="Tyr's Hand Abbey gives the Scarlet Crusade a quieter place for worship and martial teaching. The Scarlet Basilica rises over the city's skyline, while the abbey follows a design familiar from Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. Its Main Hall stands between the Hall of Arms and Library Wing. Though horrors plague the land, the Crusade keeps the abbey in careful repair and guards its cloisters fiercely from outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Tyr's Hand Abbey used for?",a="The abbey gives the Scarlet Crusade in Tyr's Hand a place to worship, live, train, and study. The grand Basilica hosts major ceremonies, while the Hall of Arms and Library Wing support its other work.",al={"what is this building","tyrs hand abbey purpose","what happens in the abbey"}},{q="Why does it look like Northshire Abbey?",a="Northshire Abbey and Tyr's Hand Abbey follow familiar Lordaeron and Stormwind designs for Holy Light monasteries. Each has a main assembly hall, a martial training wing, and an archive of sacred texts.",al={"northshire clone","why does it look like northshire","abbey layout"}},{q="Who controls the abbey right now?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls the abbey. Crusader soldiers, priests, and paladins fiercely defend Tyr's Hand, attacking anyone who does not bear their colors.",al={"who owns tyrs hand abbey","is scarlet crusade here"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For a holy warrior, Tyr's Hand Abbey shows how the Silver Hand's legacy has been corrupted. A once-hallowed place of prayer now serves fanaticism and bloodlust.",["class:Priest"]="The Library Wing holds remnants of classical Holy Light doctrine, preserved through the Scarlet Crusade's skewed and obsessive view."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","hall of arms","library wing","scarlet basilica","scarlet crusade","tyr's hand abbey","tyrs hand"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-hand","subzone:scarlet-basilica","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:northshire-abbey","zone:easternplaguelands"},src={"Tyr's Hand Abbey"}}
E["subzone:undercroft"] = {t="subzone",n="Undercroft",z="easternplaguelands",s="In the southwestern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, undead trolls have taken an old Lordaeron tomb. Zaeldarr the Outcast commands them, and a false grave in the catacombs bears Tirion Fordring’s name.",h="In the southwestern hills of the Eastern Plaguelands, undead trolls have taken an old Lordaeron tomb.",sec={{t="A Desecrated Sepulcher",b="You find the Undercroft carved into the bluffs southwest of Corin's Crossing. Lordaeron built it for its honored dead, but the kingdom's fall left the tomb open to undead trolls. Zaeldarr the Outcast leads them from its underground halls. They stalk the Plaguelands and raid the grave pits at Light's Hope Chapel, taking newly buried corpses for their grim practices.",sp=0},{t="A Pretender's Tomb",b="A false grave in the Undercroft bears Tirion Fordring's name. After his trial for treason and exile, Tirion's allies arranged a symbolic burial. This let his family keep their standing while he went into hiding. A personal memento from Tirion's past lies hidden within the grave, where only those who know the truth would search.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Undercroft?",a="Undercroft lies in the southwestern Eastern Plaguelands. Lordaeron built the burial crypt for its nobility and fallen soldiers, but undead horrors occupy it now.",al={"where is undercroft","what is this crypt","undercroft epl"}},{q="Who occupies the crypt now?",a="Undead trolls occupy the crypt under Zaeldarr the Outcast, a massive undead dire troll. They use its tunnels as a lair between raids across the region.",al={"who is inside undercroft","undercroft mobs","trolls in undercroft"}},{q="Why are there undead trolls in the Eastern Plaguelands?",a="Troll tribes such as the Mossflayer and Witherbark dwell near northern Lordaeron, where the Scourge chiefly raised humans and elves. Undead trolls like Zaeldarr and his followers roam the bluffs. They pillage burial sites and prey on unwary travelers.",al={"why trolls here","zaeldarr lore","undead trolls epl"}},{q="Why is Tirion Fordring's name on a grave here?",a="Tirion Fordring's grave at Undercroft is false. After the Alliance of Lordaeron stripped him of rank and exiled him, his allies arranged a mock burial. His family could preserve their honor while he hid in secret.",al={"tirion grave","is tirion dead","fordring tomb"}},{q="Why do the Undercroft trolls raid Light's Hope Chapel?",a="Zaeldarr the Outcast leads raids on the grave pits outside Light's Hope Chapel to steal newly buried corpses. His band uses them to bolster its ranks or feed its morbid appetites.",al={"zaeldarr raids","grave pit raid","trolls light's hope"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you find Tirion Fordring's tragic mock burial at Undercroft, alongside Zaeldarr's brood desecrating sacred crypts.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you may see Zaeldarr and his undead kindred as a grim mockery of troll traditions and the sacred rites owed to the dead."},kw={"crypt","dire troll","eastern plaguelands","grave","light's hope","the outcast","tirion fordring","undercroft","zaeldarr"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","npc:tirion-fordring","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","topic:troll","topic:light"},src={"Undercroft"}}
E["subzone:zul-mashar"] = {t="subzone",n="Zul'Mashar",z="easternplaguelands",s="In northeastern Eastern Plaguelands, the Mossflayers cling to Zul'Mashar and its ruins. Their ancient capital was broken by wars with human kingdoms, then ravaged by the Plague of Undeath.",h="In northeastern Eastern Plaguelands, the Mossflayers cling to Zul'Mashar and its ruins.",sec={{t="A Falling Stronghold",b="Before the Scourge crossed northern Lordaeron, Zul'Mashar was the seat of power for the Mossflayer forest trolls. Years of border skirmishes with Lordaeron's humans broke their lands into fragments. Then the Plague of Undeath swept through the region, striking trolls and humans alike.\n\nMazra'Alor's great stepped ziggurat still rises above the ruins, though little else remains of the capital's former glory. Warlord Thresh'jin and Zul'Brin Warpbranch command the surviving trolls, who cling to their ancient home. Many do not see the Scourge beginning to turn their own kin into rotting monstrosities.",sp=0},{t="Infiltration from the Shadows",b="Within Zul'Mashar, a threat creeps through the Mossflayers' ranks. They guard their ziggurat and struggle to keep their independence in the ruined north, while hidden agents move among them and rot spreads. Infiltrator Hameya scouts among the ruins as living warriors gradually succumb to undeath.\n\nNo grand battle marks the end of this struggle. The once-proud stronghold edges toward falling under the Lich King's sway.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Zul'Mashar?",a="The Mossflayer forest trolls hold Zul'Mashar under Warlord Thresh'jin and Zul'Brin Warpbranch. Their grip weakens as the undead plague spreads through their society.",al={"who lives in zulmashar","zul mashar rulers","mossflayer leaders"}},{q="What is Mazra'Alor?",a="Mazra'Alor is the stepped troll ziggurat within Zul'Mashar. It is the architectural heart and spiritual center of the Mossflayer tribe's ancestral capital.",al={"mazraalor","zul mashar pyramid","troll ziggurat epl"}},{q="Why is Zul'Mashar in ruins?",a="Long conflicts with Lordaeron's human kingdom wore Zul'Mashar down, and the Plague of Undeath ravaged it. The blight ruined the surrounding land, leaving the Mossflayers isolated and weakened.",al={"why is zulmashar destroyed","what happened to zul mashar"}},{q="Are the trolls here allied with the Scourge?",a="No. The living Mossflayers fight outsiders to protect their ancestral lands. Meanwhile, the Scourge secretly infects and converts their people into undead.",al={"are mossflayers scourge","trolls working with scourge"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="As a Darkspear troll, you can see the Mossflayers' plight at Zul'Mashar as a grim warning to isolated tribes that cling to ancient hatreds instead of finding allies in a changing world.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may watch Zul'Mashar with wary pragmatism, wondering whether the decaying Mossflayers will resist or swell the Scourge's ranks as zombified forest trolls."},kw={"eastern plaguelands","forest troll","hameya","mazra'alor","mossflayer","thresh'jin","warpbranch","zul'mashar"},rel={"zone:easternplaguelands","topic:troll","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Zul'Mashar"}}
E["zone:easternplaguelands"] = {t="zone",n="Eastern Plaguelands",z="easternplaguelands",s="Scourge blight darkens the Eastern Plaguelands. Stratholme remains an undead stronghold, while the Scarlet Crusade fortifies the east. Light's Hope Chapel offers neutral refuge to those who fight back.",h="Scourge blight darkens the Eastern Plaguelands.",sec={{t="A Land in Ruin",b="Once called the Eastweald, the Eastern Plaguelands were Lordaeron's fertile heartland. Stratholme anchored the region, with prosperous towns like Darrowshire and Corin's Crossing nearby. During the Third War, Prince Arthas purged Stratholme after learning its grain had been laced with the Plague of Undeath.\n\nAfter Lordaeron fell, Scourge magic spread unchecked. The soil turned brown and rotten. Ordinary plants warped into colossal mushrooms, and orange mist settled over the valleys.",sp=0},{t="A War on Three Fronts",b="Stratholme is the Scourge's southern seat of power in Lordaeron. Baron Rivendare commands it under the direction of the lich Kel'Thuzad. In the southeast, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade has fortified Tyr's Hand and assaults Stratholme's scarlet strongholds.\n\nThe Crusade's hatred reaches beyond the undead to any living traveler who crosses its borders. Farther north, the Mossflayer forest trolls of Zul'Mashar wage isolated, desperate campaigns amid the wider conflict.",sp=0},{t="Bastions of the Living",b="Watch your footing in the Eastern Plaguelands. The neutral Argent Dawn keeps Light's Hope Chapel in the far east, where Alliance and Horde champions can find shelter, supplies, and flight routes. Beyond the chapel, ruined watchtowers mark Lordaeron's lost defenses: Crown Guard, Eastwall, Northpass, and Plaguewood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What caused the sky and trees to look so sick?",a="The Cult of the Damned's Plague of Undeath left its mark across the land. After the Third War, its necromantic magic blighted the earth, changed local wildlife, and filled the air with unnatural orange smog. Forests twisted into fungal groves such as the Plaguewood.",al={"why is the sky orange","why giant mushrooms","eastern plaguelands corruption"}},{q="Where can I find a safe haven or flight path here?",a="Light's Hope Chapel, on the zone's eastern edge, is the main sanctuary. The Argent Dawn maintains it and offers flight paths to Undercity, Ironforge, Chillwind Camp, and the Hinterlands for Alliance and Horde travelers.",al={"epl safe zone","where is flight path epl","friendly town eastern plaguelands"}},{q="Who controls the city of Stratholme?",a="War divides Stratholme. Baron Rivendare rules most of its burning ruins for Kel'Thuzad, while the Scarlet Crusade holds an aggressive garrison in the western district. There, it wages a bloody siege against the undead.",al={"who leads stratholme","stratholme bosses lore","what is in stratholme"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile to outside adventurers?",a="The Scarlet Crusade's zealotry and paranoia grew after Lordaeron fell and the Silver Hand fractured. Its members believe outsiders carry the plague or consort with the undead, so they attack those who approach strongholds such as Tyr's Hand.",al={"why does scarlet crusade attack me","tyrs hand hostile","scarlet crusade red"}},{q="What happened to the town of Darrowshire?",a="During the Third War, Scourge forces led by the death knight Marduk the Black and the ghoul Horgus the Ravager attacked Darrowshire. Paladin Davil Crokford and Captain Joseph Redpath fought valiantly, but necromancy corrupted Redpath's soul and made him slaughter his own people. Darrowshire now lies in haunted ruins.",al={"darrowshire lore","fall of darrowshire","who destroyed darrowshire"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Lordaeron's fall weighs heavily on the Silver Hand. Stratholme is where Arthas turned to darkness, and Light's Hope Chapel saw a valiant last stand.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Eastern Plaguelands as the Scourge's birthplace and a frontline where the Forsaken strike against their former masters and the Scarlet zealots.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, you enter the Plaguelands on a solemn pilgrimage to reclaim and honor the devastated remnants of your former northern allies.",["profession:Herbalism"]="You can gather rare, volatile herbs in this blighted region, including Arthas' Tears, Plaguebloom, and Black Lotus.",["profession:Mining"]="Truesilver, Mithril, and Rich Thorium veins lie across the corrupted hillsides and dangerous valleys infested by the Scourge."},kw={"argent dawn","darrowshire","eastern plaguelands","kelthuzad","lights hope chapel","nathanos","plaguewood","rivendare","scarlet crusade","scourge","stratholme","tyrs hand"},rel={"zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:stratholme","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","subzone:darrowshire","subzone:plaguewood","subzone:corin-s-crossing","subzone:marris-stead","subzone:thondroril-river"},src={"Eastern Plaguelands (Classic)","Eastern Plaguelands"}}
